}, "overview": "Republican Governor Kelly Ayotte seeks a second term against Democrat Cinde Warmington, with independent Jon Kiper also on the ballot. Every poll since spring has shown Ayotte ahead, with recent surveys from Saint Anselm, YouGov, and NYT/Siena putting her lead between seven and eleven points. Analysts mostly rate the race Likely Republican, and prediction markets price Warmington's chances at roughly five percent.\n\nNew Hampshire leans slightly Democratic overall, but incumbent governors have historically been hard to beat, and Ayotte has drawn positive coverage as a Republican performing strongly in a battleground state. Warmington has campaigned on affordability and faced questions about her lobbying past while challenging Ayotte on tariffs. Unless the closing argument moves undecided voters sharply, Ayotte enters the final weeks as a clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -8.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0698, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0784, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1135, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0954, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0873, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0914, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1036, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0759, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0785, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0513, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11"